Z||000000||Pilrulz||11-06-2001||08:44 PM||||okay, why, does a duke rev like a brick, when it shares the same bore x stroke measurements as the supposedly revvy and fur chevy 302 (67-69 camaro z/28)?  <P>is the duke in any way related to above engine?<P>let's say a duke has sat in a garage for 8-10 years, and same engine has had the crank ground, and (here's the killer, at least for a duke) has been bored out slightly.  is this engine worth purchasing? (came out of blue 87 fiero)<P>let's say that the iron duke does not defeat napoleon at waterloo.  Would napoleon go on to conquer the planet... (only history buffs will understand)<P>                          pil   ||||reg||12
Z||000001||erikred||11-07-2001||10:52 AM||||The Iron Duke in it's original form (Chevy II 153) was designed from the Chevy I6 engine. The SBC was also designed after the I6. Pontiac later modified the design of the Chevy II 153 and made it into the Pontiac 151. Some things were changed such as bore and stroke, and some stayed the same. Many parts enterchange between the SBC, I6, 153, and 151 and do not forget about the marine 181 which is a 153 with larger bore and longer stroke.||||reg||10
